  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared under RBC-RAD-07. Four studies are booked (appt-00001, -00006 and -00008 are cancelled and were skipped).\n\n- pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0001): No contrast reaction on record. Diet-controlled diabetes. His last creatinine was more than 30 days old, so I ordered one to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0005). Later an outside result arrived: creatinine 1.52 on 10/22 (was 0.94 on 9/24), eGFR about 64. This doesn't meet the policy's definition of acute kidney injury, so the plan is unchanged: no IV fluids, no metformin issue, and the pre-scan creatinine order stays. Patient messaged; task-t0028 for you to review the rise.\n- pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0002): The 2019 radiology report from the day of the reaction grades it moderate (hives, eyelid swelling), even though the allergy list says \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\". Premedication ordered: prednisone 50 mg at 20:00 10/25 and at 02:00 and 08:00 10/26 (mr-t0007), plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 (mr-t0008). He needs a driver. A corrected lab result then arrived: his 10/14 creatinine is 2.8, not 0.98 (the 0.98 was another patient's sample), so eGFR is about 24. I added 0.9% saline 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0019). The CT order text still quotes the old 0.98; the note doc-t0023 records the correction. He was messaged in Spanish and English, then sent a correction (comm-t0021) withdrawing \"kidney test normal\" and asking him to arrive at 7:45. Task-t0027 for you to work up the low kidney function.\n- pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0003): The 10/4 ED visit documented acute kidney injury that hadn't resolved. Ordered:\n  - a pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0006)\n  - saline 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0009)\n  - metformin put on hold (mr-00392): no doses on 10/26 and for at least 48 hours after, restart only after a normal recheck. The recheck creatinine is ordered for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0011), with task-t0012 to decide on restart.\n  \n  A 2022 outside report then arrived showing a moderate reaction to iopamidol, so I added premedication: prednisone 50 mg at 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00 10/26 (mr-t0017), plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00 (mr-t0018). She needs a driver. First message comm-t0013, updated message comm-t0022. Iopamidol isn't in the catalog, so it isn't on her allergy list yet; task-t0029 to add it.\n- pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00, CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast, stone protocol (sr-t0004): Ordered as booked; no prep needed and she was told so. A 2024 outside report of a mild reaction to iohexol arrived and is now on her allergy list (alg-t0020); it doesn't affect this scan.\n\nThere is a progress note for each patient (doc-t0023 to t0026). I closed the four results that arrived while I worked (inbox-a0001 to a0004). Older inbox items for other patients were left alone.",
